    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Admiringglance Willy(Dominic West)recognises thetalentofColette (KeiraKnightley)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 123.813, 617.624, 219.308, 675.176 ],
    "font" : "BentonModernTwo-Roman",
    "font size" : 6.968,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Willy is a “literary entrepreneur”. He has no qualms about putting his name on Colette’s semi-autobiographical stories andbaskinginwhatshouldbeher glory. West plays him as a flamboyant and likeable ﬁgure with a ﬂairformarketing."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 37,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 331.733, 624.717, 427.267, 660.92 ],
    "font" : "BentonModernTwo-Roman",
    "font size" : 6.968,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "The New York scenes are followed by a large section set in rural Andalusia, where the locals endure equally complicated emotionallives."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
